The Unreleased section filed everything under '### Fixed', including a new
public CLI surface and a removal. A reader pricing the release off the
section headings would conclude 0.7.1; the content is a minor bump.

- '### Added': 'tracker textconv <file>' is a real subcommand. It did not
  exist before this cycle -- the .gitattributes diff driver named it and
  only the hypergumbo-tracker-textconv console script was ever built.
- '### Removed': setup.py's 'git config --global' fallback, which leaked a
  per-repo diff driver into the user's machine-wide git config.

Both were buried mid-paragraph inside a Fixed entry. The '--global' clause
is trimmed from that entry so the fact has one home rather than two.

